there's been a ton of hype for the  iphone 14 lineup coming later this year  especially thanks to some major changes  and differences like the new dual cutout  face id sensors instead of the notch and  some absolutely huge changes in the  camera features however we just got some  absolutely terrible news about the  lineup yes we just got a report from  nikkei asia saying that at least one  iphone 14 model is three weeks behind  schedule due to the china lockdowns so  what i'm gonna do in this video is  explain exactly why and how we got to  this point why apple is so far behind  with the iphone 14 lineup how they could  potentially  fix it and deliver the iphone 14 lineup  on time in september and i'm also going  to share the latest brand new leaks and  rumors that we just got so without  further ado let's jump into this new  report according to the supply chain  sources who spoke to nikkei asia they  said it's challenging to make up for the  lost time now of course they're talking  about all the lockdowns that have been  happening in shanghai and in general in  china since sometime in march they said  apple and its suppliers are working  around the clock to speed up development  adding that the pace of reopening in  shanghai is rather slow and because of  that it seems like apple has fallen  three weeks behind in terms of the  iphone 14 lineup schedule and that's  very important because apple has a very  tight lock on the schedule they do  things like right before  the iphone actually gets a release is  when they start the mass production so  if they're behind by three weeks this  means we could realistically get late  iphones this year but the interesting  detail to look at is that it could be at  least one iphone 14 model that gets  delayed which means that maybe some of  them come on time and then some of them  come a little bit later and  interestingly the reason for that is  because there are certain suppliers like  china's luxury precision industry that  have orders to build two out of the four  models this year so there are different  companies that work on different models  and the reason this is such a serious  deal right now is that although shanghai  has recently loosened their lockdowns  there are still some neighborhood  enforcers that are keeping large parts  of shanghai  in lockdown despite the actual official  easing of the lockdowns that are  happening right now so who knows what's  going gonna be happening and adding to  that on may 6 we actually got some  security footage released of an apple  plant in i believe it was uh the quanta  plant in shanghai  of the workers actually riding and  jumping over the security checkpoints  over there so i'm not going to show the  video but it was pretty crazy to see and  earlier this month ming chi kuo who has  been a reliable apple analyst for many  years he's basically famous in the apple  tech space he reported earlier this  month may 4th that june through august  is going to be critical for ramping up  new iphone production because if the  lockdowns aren't removed before june  then the iphone production capacity  likely including iphone 14 may still be  affected by logistics and workforce  allocation and making things even worse  he said that china's policies could have  a more significant impact on consumer  electronics on the demand side than the  production side saying that there could  actually be a recession with demand  going down because people are focusing  on their necessities like food water  medicine instead of actually spending  money on consumer electronics so that  could be an even bigger issue out of all  of these supply chain disruptions and  adding on to that just a couple of days  ago he said that many companies and  investors expect improved production  after shanghai actually reopens however  he said his latest survey indicates that  there is already some evidence that  lowering consumer confidence and  worsening inflation is weakening and  destroying consumer electronics demand  and that actually includes apple  products with the demand disappearing  not deferring and this is actually a  really big deal because it impacts  china's gdp numbers directly and that is  exactly what matters in terms of seeing  if they're in a recession or not because  if they are going into a recession  that's going to impact everything in  china from the supply side to the  production side everything and check out  this report from jpmorgan yesterday they  said we downgraded our china gdp  forecast again now looking for second  quarter gdp to contract negative 5.4  percent compared to their previous  estimate of negative 1.5 that is a  absolutely terrible estimate showing  that they are likely going to be going  into recession and they even said that  their quarter two global growth forecast  stands at just 0.6  growth that's the global economy which  means that we could be getting close to  a global recession saying that it's  easily the weakest quarter since the  great financial crisis outside of 2020.  and now if you think this is just  isolated to china it could actually be  an issue here in the united states as  well because in the first quarter of  2022 our us gdp dropped by 1.4  that means we actually had a quarter  that was negative so if this current  second quarter is negative that means we  will technically be in a recession for  the first half of this year and maybe  even longer and check this out just this  morning atlanta fed's gdp now estimate  for real gdp growth in q2 is 1.8  down from 2.4 on may 18th that's just  one week ago so we are now just 1.8  percent from a recession and the reason  this is such a big deal is because  previously before we got that really bad  negative 1.4 percent readout for quarter  one the estimate was brought down from  1.3 percent on april 19th all the way  down to 0.4  on april 26th within two weeks  everything changed from an estimate of  plus 1.3 all the way to negative 1.4  which is a massive deal so this 1.8  estimate for the second quarter could  change very quickly and now getting back  to china things got even worse for the  iphone 14 lineup earlier this month  because on may 4th foxconn abruptly  halted hiring at the iphone factory amid  a new lockdown and iphone 14 delay  concern so that's even worse for the  iphone because they just stopped hiring  because of the new lockdown so it's just  such a bad thing over there but luckily  just a couple of days ago apple actually  asked foxconn to start iphone recruiting  or hiring  two months early like this is completely  unique they are probably so worried  about the iphone 14s getting delayed  that they're actually hiring two months  in advance to make sure they can build  up a stock and not have to delay the  iphone and if you didn't already know  apple actually did delay the iphone two  years ago in  2020 because on july 30th apple  confirmed that the new iphones would not  arrive in september and that was a huge  shock to a lot of people and of course  those delays were once again from  lockdowns that happened and basically  slowed everything down and the crazier  thing is they not only delayed the  iphone 12 lineup but they delayed half  of them for another month so it wasn't  until november 13th when you could  actually buy the iphone 12 mini and the  12 pro max and that definitely impacted  sales and that really sucked for me  because i bought the 12 pro max and i  had to wait a couple of months extra  compared to the usual september release  date until i could actually get my hands  on that iphone so going back to the  original article there's a chance that  if some delays happen we could actually  get like a half release with two of the  models getting released on time and two  of them getting delayed just like it  happened in 2020 and in my opinion the  one model that i think is going to get  delayed is the new iphone 14 max model  which basically has basic features but  the larger 6.7 inch size with the notch  because that's going to be a new design  that apple hasn't really done before  with the aluminum chassis and the  regular features so there might be more  delays in terms of that model so i think  what kind of makes sense is apple could  have the regular iphone 14 model and  then the iphone 14 pro max so the people  who want the iphone 14 max they could be  tempted to actually upgrade to the 14  pro max model instead of waiting for  that regular max model that could come a  month later alongside the regular 6.1  inch iphone 14 pro model but once again  hopefully apple's move of hiring workers  two months early completely stops all  these delays and we actually get all of  them in september now i do want to go  through some new leaks and changes in  rumors because i think these new iphones  are going to be absolutely incredible  now first of all from page tech just  came out with a new video showing off  some new exclusive renders by ian's  elbow showing off this new purple color  which i think is very very subtle but it  does look pretty nice honestly and as  you can see we have the new dual hole  punch cutout which i think looks awesome  we have the new thinner bezels and in  this render you can actually see the  sensors that are behind it we have the  camera we have i believe the dot  projector combo right here and  potentially the infrared camera right  there and then he also showed off these  other angles with the actual camera and  man looking at these renders i am so  excited for the iphone 14 pro models i  mean this just looks so incredibly clean  and if you think the new purple pro  color sounds crazy well it looks like  all of the rumors and leaks are adding  up and it's most likely that we are  getting a new purple color option  because we got some leaks from chinese  social media site weibo basically  showing that purple is the most likely  new option but moving on to some new  leaked features that we should expect  mischief did say last month that the  iphone 14 models will likely feature  upgraded front cameras with autofocus  and very recently we saw that all iphone  14 models are gonna gain two  front-facing camera upgrades of course  that's the autofocus and the wider f 1.9  aperture which is basically gonna  increase the light input that comes into  the sensor and give you sharper better  photos with less noise and i think  that's going to be a huge deal and then  on top of that we actually got  confirmation from ross young that he  believes that the new iphone displays  for the pro models are going to match  the new ones that are on the samsung's  which means that they can refresh down  to one hertz refresh rate instead of the  current 10 hertz on the 13 pro model so  that's gonna go from one hertz to 120  hertz with promotion and because of that  there is a chance that apple could  finally be giving us an always-on  display mode which i've been asking for  for years now so hopefully we get that  and the last thing i want to show you  guys before i finish up this video is my  personal thoughts on hopefully this new  bronze slash copper finish because i  think this would be a much better choice  from apple to give us this bronze color  compared to the new purple which  honestly doesn't look that much  different compared to the current blue  that we have which honestly i don't  really like so  if we get this bronze color i think that  would sell a lot of the pro models so  there you guys go hopefully you enjoy  this video and if you completely  disagree and you don't think that the  iphones are getting delayed let me know  down below but if you enjoyed the video  click the circle about to subscribe and  definitely check out one of those two  right over there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]

